"Direction to '%4$s' would give an AUC of %5$s, with sensitivity and "
"specificity swapped. • Change it only if that matches what the marker means "
"clinically — the outcome coding is worth checking too."
msgstr ""

#: R/enhancedROC.b.R
msgid ""
"%1$s has an AUC of %2$s, below the 0.5 expected from a coin toss, but its "
"confidence interval still crosses 0.5. • About half of markers carrying no "
"information at all fall below 0.5 by chance, so this is not evidence that "
"the marker runs backwards. • It is consistent with a marker that simply does "
"not discriminate. • If you expected it to run the other way, check the "
"Direction setting and the outcome coding before drawing any conclusion."
msgstr ""

