msgstr "<h5>Pozitif Öngörü Değeri (PÖD)</h5>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<i>Number Needed to Screen</i> counts entries into the pathway, that is "
"first tests only. A serial strategy also performs a second test on part of "
"that group; the Cost Analysis table shows the expected number of each test."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><b>Adequate Information:</b> Precision and power depend strongly on the "
"number of discordant pairs</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><b>Available Cases:</b> Standalone metrics use each test's observed "
"reference/test pairs; paired comparisons use common determinate rows</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><b>Binary Recoding:</b> Each test is analyzed after positive/negative "
"recoding; multilevel results require explicit handling when indeterminate "
"values should be excluded</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><b>Gold Standard:</b> Reference test must represent true disease status "
"(e.g., biopsy, final diagnosis)</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><b>Paired Data:</b> All tests must be performed on the same "
"patients/samples (not independent groups)</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>1SE Rule</strong>: Selects the most parsimonious model within 1 "
"SE of minimum CV error.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>1SE Kuralı</strong>: Minimum ÇD hatasının 1 SE içindeki en yalın "
"modeli seçer.</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Choose Tests to Compare:</strong> Select 2-3 diagnostic tests "
"you want to evaluate</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Clinical Research:</strong> Validating biomarkers, imaging "
"techniques, or clinical assessments</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Confidence Intervals:</strong> The per-test CI tables report "
"Clopper-Pearson exact intervals for the proportions (sensitivity, "
"specificity, PPV, NPV, accuracy and prevalence), as computed by "
"epiR::epi.tests() with its default settings. Likelihood ratios are reported "
"as point estimates only, without confidence intervals. The Overall Percent "
"Agreement (OPA) table uses the selected single-proportion method. Paired "
"differences use Newcombe's method-10 score interval for correlated "
"proportions.</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Configure Options:</strong> Enable statistical comparisons, "
"confidence intervals, or visualizations as needed</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Convert post-test odds back to probability</strong>: Post-test P "
"= Odds/(1+Odds)</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Test sonrası odds'u tekrar olasılığa dönüştürün</strong>: Test "
"sonrası P = Odds/(1+Odds)</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Convert pre-test probability to odds</strong>: Odds = "
"P/(1-P)</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Test öncesi olasılığı odds'a dönüştürün</strong>: Odds = "
"P/(1-P)</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Copy Report:</strong> Use the auto-generated sentences for your "
"documentation</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Define Positive Levels:</strong> Specify what constitutes a "
"\"positive\" result for each test</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Elastic Net</strong>: Combines L1 and L2 penalties; useful when "
"predictors are correlated.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Elastic Net</strong>: L1 ve L2 cezalarını birleştirir; tahmin "
"ediciler korelasyonlu olduğunda yararlıdır.</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Gold Standard:</strong> Assumes your reference test is truly "
"accurate</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Lambda</strong>: Controls regularization strength. Higher lambda "
"= fewer variables selected.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Lambda</strong>: Düzenlileştirme gücünü kontrol eder. Daha "
"yüksek lambda = daha az değişken seçilir.</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Lambda</strong>: Controls regularization strength. Higher lambda "
"shrinks every coefficient further toward zero, but none reaches zero, so the "
"number of variables never changes.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Lambda</strong>: Düzenlileştirme gücünü kontrol eder. Daha "
"yüksek lambda her katsayıyı sıfıra doğru daha da daraltır ancak hiçbiri "
"sıfıra ulaşmaz, bu nedenle değişken sayısı asla değişmez.</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>McNemar Test:</strong> Requires paired/matched data for "
"statistical comparisons</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Method Comparison:</strong> Describing and testing differences "
"among paired tests</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Missing Data:</strong> Standalone estimates use available "
"reference/test pairs; paired comparisons use common determinate rows. "
"Missing-data handling and counts should be reported.</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Multiply odds by likelihood ratio</strong>: Post-test odds = "
"Pre-test odds × LR</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li><strong>Negative Likelihood Ratio (LR-)</strong>: (1-Se)/Sp</li>"
msgstr "<li><strong>Negatif Olabilirlik Oranı (LR-)</strong>: (1-Se)/Sp</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Odds Ratio</strong>: exp(coefficient). OR > 1 increases "
"probability of the positive class.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Odds Oranı</strong>: exp(katsayı). OR > 1 pozitif sınıf "
"olasılığını artırır.</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li><strong>Positive Likelihood Ratio (LR+)</strong>: Se/(1-Sp)</li>"
msgstr "<li><strong>Pozitif Olabilirlik Oranı (LR+)</strong>: Se/(1-Sp)</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li><strong>Prevalence (P)</strong>: The pre-test probability of disease</li>"
msgstr "<li><strong>Prevalans (P)</strong>: Hastalığın test öncesi olasılığı</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Prevalence Dependency:</strong> PPV and NPV vary with disease "
"prevalence</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Protocol Development:</strong> Optimizing diagnostic "
"workflows</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Quality Assessment:</strong> Measuring agreement between "
"different raters or methods</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Run Analysis:</strong> Review estimates, denominators, "
"exclusions, and statistical comparisons</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Sample Size:</strong> Results more reliable with larger, "
"representative samples</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Select Gold Standard:</strong> Choose your most reliable "
"reference test (e.g., biopsy, expert consensus)</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Sensitivity (Se)</strong>: Probability of a positive test in "
"diseased subjects</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Duyarlılık (Se)</strong>: Hastalıklı deneklerde testin pozitif "
"çıkma olasılığı</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Specificity (Sp)</strong>: Probability of a negative test in "
"non-diseased subjects</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Özgüllük (Sp)</strong>: Hastalıksız deneklerde testin negatif "
"çıkma olasılığı</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Standardization (default on):</strong> predictors are centered "
"and scaled before fitting, so the penalty treats variables with different "
"units comparably. The Coefficient and Odds Ratio columns of the Selected "
"Variables table are then back-transformed to the <strong>original "
"measurement scale</strong> (per 1 unit of a continuous predictor, or present "
"vs absent for a binary one). The Importance column and the Coefficient Plot "
"stay on the per-standard-deviation scale, which is the quantity that is "
"comparable across predictors with different units.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li><strong>Standardizasyon (varsayılan açık):</strong> tahmin ediciler "
"uyarlamadan önce merkezileştirilir ve ölçeklendirilir, böylece ceza farklı "
"birimlere sahip değişkenleri karşılaştırılabilir şekilde ele alır. Seçilen "
"Değişkenler tablosunun Katsayı ve Odds Oranı sütunları daha sonra "
"<strong>orijinal ölçüm ölçeğine</strong> geri dönüştürülür (sürekli bir "
"tahmin edicinin 1 birimi başına veya ikili bir tahmin edici için var ve "
"yok). Önem sütunu ve Katsayı Grafiği, farklı birimlere sahip tahmin ediciler "
"arasında karşılaştırılabilir olan standart sapma başına ölçekte kalır.</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li><strong>Test Validation:</strong> Comparing new diagnostic methods "
"against established standards</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Always validate the scoring system on an independent cohort before "
"clinical adoption.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Klinik benimsemeden önce puanlama sistemini her zaman bağımsız bir "
"kohortta doğrulayın.</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Bootstrap optimism correction estimates how much the apparent AUC "
"overestimates true performance.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Bootstrap iyimserlik düzeltmesi, görünürdeki EAA'nın gerçek performansı "
"ne kadar abarttığını tahmin eder.</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Combined probability = {first} + {second} = {combined}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Birleşik olasılık = {first} + {second} = {combined}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Combined probability = {sens1} + {sens2} - {both} = {combined}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Birleşik olasılık = {sens1} + {sens2} - {both} = {combined}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Combined probability = {sens1} × {sens2} = {combined}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Combined probability = {spec1} × {spec2} = {combined}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Combined sensitivity (Se) = {value}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Birleşik duyarlılık (Se) = {value}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Combined specificity (Sp) = {value}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Birleşik özgüllük (Sp) = {value}</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Comparing diagnostic accuracy of 2-3 tests performed on same "
"patients</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Continuous predictors in the scoring system are dichotomized at %s (set "
"by 'Cut Point for Continuous Predictors'); the score-based performance "
"therefore reflects a simplified point model and may differ from the "
"continuous LASSO model's AUC.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Puanlama sistemindeki sürekli tahmin ediciler %s noktasında ikiye "
"ayrılır ('Sürekli Tahmin Ediciler İçin Kesim Noktası' ile ayarlanır); bu "
"nedenle puana dayalı performans basitleştirilmiş bir puan modelini yansıtır "
"ve sürekli LASSO modelinin EAA değerinden farklı olabilir.</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Denominator = (1-P) × Sp + P × (1-Se) = {numerator} + {p} × {oneMinusSe} "
"= {denominator}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Denominator = P × Se + (1-P) × (1-Sp) = {numerator} + {oneMinusP} × "
"{oneMinusSp} = {denominator}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Emergency teaching pair (Physiologic test + "
"Biomarker)</li><li>Acute-imaging teaching pair (Clinical assessment + "
"Imaging)</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Acil eğitim çifti (Fizyolojik test + Biyobelirteç)</li><li>Akut "
"görüntüleme eğitim çifti (Klinik değerlendirme + Görüntüleme)</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Evaluating if a new test is significantly better/worse than standard "
"test</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Events-per-variable (EPV) should be >=10. Below 5, results are "
"unreliable regardless of regularization.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Değişken başına olay (EPV) >=10 olmalıdır. 5'in altında, "
"düzenlileştirmeden bağımsız olarak sonuçlar güvenilmezdir.</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Given a negative Test 1, probability of testing negative on Test 2: "
"{value}</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Negatif Test 1 verildiğinde, Test 2'de negatif test etme olasılığı: "
"{value}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Given a positive Test 1, probability of testing positive on Test 2: "
"{value}</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Pozitif Test 1 verildiğinde, Test 2'de pozitif test etme olasılığı: "
"{value}</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Higher total scores indicate higher probability of the event (positive "
"class).</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Daha yüksek toplam puanlar olayın (pozitif sınıf) daha yüksek "
"olasılığını gösterir.</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>HIV-style teaching pair (Ag/Ab assay → differentiation assay); this is "
"not a complete HIV diagnostic algorithm</li><li>Cancer-screening teaching "
"pair (Imaging → Tissue sampling)</li><li>Respiratory-infection teaching pair "
"(Rapid antigen → Molecular assay)</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Inter-observer agreement should be assessed for any morphologic scoring "
"components.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Herhangi bir morfolojik puanlama bileşeni için gözlemciler arası uyum "
"değerlendirilmelidir.</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>LASSO coefficients do not have standard errors or p-values. Use "
"bootstrap validation for inference.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>LASSO katsayılarının standart hataları veya p değerleri yoktur. Çıkarım "
"için bootstrap doğrulamasını kullanın.</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>McNemar's test compares overall accuracy only - does not separately test "
"sensitivity vs specificity differences</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>NPV = numerator/denominator = {numerator}/{denominator} = {npv}</li>"
msgstr "<li>NÖD = pay/payda = {numerator}/{denominator} = {npv}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Numerator = (1-P) × Sp = {oneMinusP} × {sp} = {numerator}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Numerator = P × Se = {p} × {se} = {numerator}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<li>Optimizing test selection based on performance metrics</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>P-values do not indicate clinical importance - consider effect sizes and "
"practical implications</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>PPV = numerator/denominator = {numerator}/{denominator} = {ppv}</li>"
msgstr "<li>PÖD = pay/payda = {numerator}/{denominator} = {ppv}</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Predictors were <strong>not</strong> standardized; coefficients, odds "
"ratios, importance, and the Coefficient Plot are all on the original "
"measurement scale of each variable.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Tahmin ediciler standardize <strong>edilmemiştir</strong>; katsayılar, "
"odds oranları, önem ve Katsayı Grafiği her değişkenin orijinal ölçüm "
"ölçeğindedir.</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Prevalence (P) = {value}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Prevalans (P) = {value}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Probability of negative Test 1 followed by positive Test 2: (1 - "
"{sens1}) × {sens2} = {value}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Probability of positive Test 1 followed by negative Test 2: (1 - "
"{spec1}) × {spec2} = {value}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Probability of testing negative on Test 1: {value}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 1'de negatif test etme olasılığı: {value}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Probability of testing negative on Test 2: {value}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 2'de negatif test etme olasılığı: {value}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Probability of testing positive on both: {sens1} × {sens2} = {both}</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Probability of testing positive on Test 1: {value}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 1'de pozitif çıkma olasılığı: {value}</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Probability of testing positive on Test 2: {value}</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 2'de pozitif çıkma olasılığı: {value}</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Requires paired observations - cannot compare tests performed on "
"different patient groups</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Rule-out teaching pair (Initial assessment → "
"Biomarker)</li><li>Exclusion teaching pair (Clinical score → Laboratory "
"assay)</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Selected variables are the features most useful for distinguishing the "
"two groups.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Seçilen değişkenler iki grubu ayırt etmek için en yararlı "
"özelliklerdir.</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Small number of discordant pairs reduces statistical power and "
"reliability</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Test negative on Test 1 but positive on Test 2</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 1'de negatif ancak Test 2'de pozitif test</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Test negative on Test 1, OR</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 1'de negatif test, VEYA</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Test positive on Test 1 but negative on Test 2</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 1'de pozitif ancak Test 2'de negatif test</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<li>Test positive on Test 1, OR</li>"
msgstr "<li>Test 1'de pozitif test, VEYA</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>The scoring system assigns positive points for features favoring the "
"event class and negative points for the reference class.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Puanlama sistemi olay sınıfını destekleyen özellikler için pozitif "
"puanlar, referans sınıf için negatif puanlar verir.</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>The scoring system rounds coefficients to integers, which loses "
"precision but gains clinical usability.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Puanlama sistemi katsayıları tam sayılara yuvarlar, bu da kesinliği "
"kaybeder ancak klinik kullanılabilirlik kazandırır.</li>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>This function cannot handle continuous test results directly for "
"statistical comparison. For continuous diagnostic tests, please use the "
"dedicated ROC (Receiver Operating Characteristic) analysis functions for "
"comparing curves (e.g., DeLong's test).</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<li>Validating diagnostic tools in clinical or pathology practice</li>"
msgstr ""

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>Variables NOT selected are not necessarily unimportant - they may be "
"redundant with selected features.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Seçilmeyen değişkenler mutlaka önemsiz değildir - seçilen özelliklerle "
"gereksiz (yedekli) olabilirler.</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>With correlated predictors, LASSO arbitrarily selects one from a group. "
"Consider elastic net (alpha 0.5).</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Korelasyonlu tahmin edicilerle LASSO bir gruptan rastgele birini seçer. "
"Elastic net (alfa 0.5) düşünün.</li>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<li>With correlated predictors, Ridge shares the coefficient among them "
"rather than picking one, which is one reason to prefer it when predictors "
"are collinear.</li>"
msgstr ""
"<li>Korelasyonlu tahmin edicilerle Ridge, birini seçmek yerine katsayıyı "
"aralarında paylaşır; bu da tahmin ediciler eşdoğrusal (collinear) olduğunda "
"bunu tercih etmenin bir nedenidir.</li>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<ol>"
msgstr "<ol>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<p><b>%1$s:</b> exact p = %2$.3f"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<p><b>%1$s:</b> χ² = %2$.2f, p = %3$.3f"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><b>Comparison:</b> %1$s (accuracy: %2$.1f%%) vs %3$s (accuracy: "
"%4$.1f%%)</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><b>Descriptive interpretation:</b> <span "
"style='color:inherit;'><b>%1$s</b></span> had the highest observed balanced "
"accuracy in this sample (overall accuracy %2$.1f%%). This descriptive "
"ranking is not a superiority test or clinical recommendation. Review the "
"pairwise comparisons above for inferential results.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<p><b>Overall comparison:</b> Cochran's Q test (χ² = %1$.2f, p = %2$.3f)"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Accuracy:</strong> Overall probability of correct "
"classification</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/cotest.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Clinical Interpretation:</strong></p>\n"
"                <p>Disease prevalence (pre-test probability): "
"<strong>%1$s</strong></p>\n"
"                <p><strong>Both tests positive:</strong> %2$s probability "
"(%3$s) - %4$s</p>\n"
"                <p><strong>Both tests negative:</strong> %5$s probability "
"(%6$s) %7$s</p>\n"
"                <p><strong>Single positive test:</strong></p>\n"
"                <ul>\n"
"                <li>%8$s positive only: <strong>%9$s</strong> %10$s</li>\n"
"                <li>%11$s positive only: <strong>%12$s</strong> %13$s</li>\n"
"                </ul>\n"
"                <div style='background-color: rgba(33, 152, 255, 0.07); "
"padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px; margin-top: 15px; color: inherit;'>\n"
"                <p><strong>Copy-ready summary:</strong></p>\n"
"                <p style='font-family: monospace; font-size: "
"12px;'>%14$s</p>\n"
"                </div>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Important:</strong> These thresholds and use cases are examples "
"only. They are not clinical guides, validated decision rules, or "
"recommendations for patient care.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<p><strong>LR-:</strong> How much negative test decreases odds of disease</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<p><strong>LR+:</strong> How much positive test increases odds of disease</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>McNemar Test:</strong> Statistical comparison between paired "
"tests</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Measured performance:</strong> %1$s had both high sensitivity "
"(%2$.1f%%) and high specificity (%3$.1f%%) in this sample: few false "
"negatives and few false positives.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Measured performance:</strong> %1$s had high sensitivity "
"(%2$.1f%%) but lower specificity (%3$.1f%%) in this sample: few false "
"negatives, more false positives.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Measured performance:</strong> %1$s had high specificity "
"(%2$.1f%%) but lower sensitivity (%3$.1f%%) in this sample: few false "
"positives, more false negatives.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Measured performance:</strong> %1$s reached neither 95%% "
"sensitivity (%2$.1f%%) nor 95%% specificity (%3$.1f%%) in this sample, so at "
"this operating point it produces both false negatives and false positives at "
"a rate you can read off the Decision Test Comparison table. These are the "
"rates observed in these particular cases, not a fixed property of the "
"test.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Measured performance:</strong> sensitivity and/or specificity "
"could not be computed for %s because one gold-standard class has no cases, "
"so that rate has an empty denominator. This test is named here only because "
"the ranking had nothing else to compare; check the 2x2 counts in the Recoded "
"Data table before reading any other panel.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<p><strong>NPV:</strong> Probability of no disease when test negative</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "<p><strong>PPV:</strong> Probability of disease when test positive</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Sensitivity:</strong> Probability test is positive when disease "
"present (rule-out ability)</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p><strong>Specificity:</strong> Probability test is negative when disease "
"absent (rule-in ability)</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>Calculation steps:</p>"
msgstr "<p>Hesaplama adımları:</p>"

#: R/psychopdaROC.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>Dot plots aren't available in combined plot mode. Please uncheck 'Combine "
"plots' to view individual dot plots.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Nokta grafikleri birleştirilmiş grafik modunda kullanılamaz. Bireysel "
"nokta grafiklerini görüntülemek için lütfen 'Grafikleri birleştir' işaretini "
"kaldırın.</p>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>Elastic Net blends the L1 (LASSO) and L2 (Ridge) penalties, here with a "
"mixing weight of alpha = %.2f. The L1 part can shrink coefficients exactly "
"to zero, so some variable selection still happens, while the L2 part keeps "
"correlated predictors together instead of letting the model pick one of them "
"arbitrarily.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Elastic Net, burada alfa = %.2f karışım ağırlığı ile L1 (LASSO) ve L2 "
"(Ridge) cezalarını harmanlar. L1 kısmı katsayıları tam olarak sıfıra "
"daraltabilir, böylece bir miktar değişken seçimi devam eder; L2 kısmı ise "
"modelin bunlardan birini rastgele seçmesine izin vermek yerine korelasyonlu "
"tahmin edicileri bir arada tutar.</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>For a subject to test negative in this strategy, they must either:</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir deneğin bu stratejide negatif test sonucu vermesi için şunlardan biri "
"olmalıdır:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>For a subject to test negative in this strategy, they must test negative "
"on both tests:</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir deneğin bu stratejide negatif test sonucu vermesi için her iki testte "
"de negatif çıkması gerekir:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>For a subject to test positive in this strategy, they must either:</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir deneğin bu stratejide pozitif test sonucu vermesi için şunlardan biri "
"olmalıdır:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>For a subject to test positive in this strategy, they must test positive "
"on at least one test. This is calculated using the complement of the "
"probability of testing negative on both tests:</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir deneğin bu stratejide pozitif test sonucu vermesi için en az bir "
"testte pozitif çıkması gerekir. Bu, her iki testte de negatif çıkma "
"olasılığının tümleyeni kullanılarak hesaplanır:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>For a subject to test positive in this strategy, they must test positive "
"on both tests:</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir deneğin bu stratejide pozitif test sonucu vermesi için her iki testte "
"de pozitif çıkması gerekir:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>How much more likely a negative test result is to occur in patients with "
"disease compared to those without:</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Negatif bir test sonucunun hastalığı olanlarda olmayanlara kıyasla ortaya "
"çıkma olasılığının ne kadar daha fazla olduğu:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>How much more likely a positive test result is to occur in patients with "
"disease compared to those without:</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Pozitif bir test sonucunun hastalığı olanlarda olmayanlara kıyasla ortaya "
"çıkma olasılığının ne kadar daha fazla olduğu:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>In this strategy, both tests are performed on all subjects. A subject is "
"considered positive if either test is positive.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bu stratejide her iki test de tüm deneklere uygulanır. Herhangi bir test "
"pozitifse denek pozitif kabul edilir.</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>In this strategy, the second test is only performed if the first test is "
"negative. A subject is considered positive if either test is positive.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bu stratejide ikinci test yalnızca ilk test negatifse uygulanır. Herhangi "
"bir test pozitifse denek pozitif kabul edilir.</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>In this strategy, the second test is only performed if the first test is "
"positive. A subject is considered positive only if both tests are "
"positive.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bu stratejide ikinci test yalnızca ilk test pozitifse uygulanır. Bir "
"denek yalnızca her iki test de pozitifse pozitif kabul edilir.</p>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>LASSO (Least Absolute Shrinkage and Selection Operator) adds an L1 "
"penalty to the logistic regression likelihood, which shrinks some "
"coefficients exactly to zero. This performs automatic variable selection, "
"identifying the most important predictors for your binary outcome.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>LASSO (En Küçük Mutlak Daralma ve Seçim Operatörü), lojistik regresyon "
"olabilirliğine bazı katsayıları tam olarak sıfıra daraltan bir L1 cezası "
"ekler. Bu, otomatik değişken seçimi gerçekleştirerek ikili sonucunuz için en "
"önemli tahmin edicileri tanımlar.</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>LR- = (1 - {se}) / {sp} = {lr}</p>"
msgstr "<p>LR- = (1 - {se}) / {sp} = {lr}</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>LR- = (1 - Sensitivity) / Specificity</p>"
msgstr "<p>LR- = (1 - Duyarlılık) / Özgüllük</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>LR+ = {se} / (1 - {sp}) = {lr}</p>"
msgstr "<p>LR+ = {se} / (1 - {sp}) = {lr}</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>LR+ = Sensitivity / (1 - Specificity)</p>"
msgstr "<p>LR+ = Duyarlılık / (1 - Özgüllük)</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>NPV = ((1-P) × Sp) / ((1-P) × Sp + P × (1-Se))</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>PPV = (P × Se) / (P × Se + (1-P) × (1-Sp))</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>Probability calculation:</p>"
msgstr "<p>Olasılık hesaplaması:</p>"

#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>Ridge regression adds an L2 penalty to the logistic regression "
"likelihood. It shrinks coefficients toward zero but never "
"<strong>to</strong> zero, so it does <strong>not</strong> perform variable "
"selection: every predictor you supplied is retained in the model. Ridge is "
"the right choice when you believe most predictors carry some signal, or when "
"they are strongly correlated and you want the penalty shared among them "
"rather than one arbitrarily kept.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Ridge regresyonu lojistik regresyon olabilirliğine bir L2 cezası ekler. "
"Katsayıları sıfıra doğru daraltır ancak asla sıfıra <strong>kadar</strong> "
"daraltmaz, bu nedenle değişken seçimi <strong>yapmaz</strong>: sağladığınız "
"her tahmin edici modelde tutulur. Çoğu tahmin edicinin bir miktar sinyal "
"taşıdığına inandığınızda veya güçlü bir şekilde korelasyonlu olduklarında ve "
"cezanın birinin rastgele tutulması yerine aralarında paylaşılmasını "
"istediğinizde Ridge doğru seçimdir.</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>Se<sub>combined</sub> = 1 - (1-Se<sub>1</sub>) × (1-Se<sub>2</sub>)</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>Se<sub>combined</sub> = Se<sub>1</sub> + (1-Se<sub>1</sub>) × "
"Se<sub>2</sub></p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>Se<sub>combined</sub> = Se<sub>1</sub> + Se<sub>2</sub> - (Se<sub>1</sub> "
"× Se<sub>2</sub>)</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>Se<sub>combined</sub> = Se<sub>1</sub> × Se<sub>2</sub></p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>Sp<sub>combined</sub> = Sp<sub>1</sub> + (1-Sp<sub>1</sub>) × "
"Sp<sub>2</sub></p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>Sp<sub>combined</sub> = Sp<sub>1</sub> × Sp<sub>2</sub></p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/cotest.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>Tests are modeled with conditional dependence:<br>\n"
"                Dependence for subjects with disease: %1$.2f<br>\n"
"                Dependence for subjects without disease: %2$.2f<br>\n"
"                Realized phi (disease): %3$s<br>\n"
"                Realized phi (no disease): %4$s<br>\n"
"                <span style='font-size: 90%%;'>(Phi is the correlation "
"between the two test results\n"
"                actually achieved by the fitted model, on a −1 to +1 scale, "
"where 0 is\n"
"                conditional independence. It differs from the value you "
"entered when that value\n"
"                was not attainable given the sensitivities and specificities "
"supplied.)</span></p>\n"
"                <p>Joint probabilities after accounting for dependence:<br>\n"
"                P(Test1+,Test2+ | Disease+): %5$.4f<br>\n"
"                P(Test1+,Test2- | Disease+): %6$.4f<br>\n"
"                P(Test1-,Test2+ | Disease+): %7$.4f<br>\n"
"                P(Test1-,Test2- | Disease+): %8$.4f<br>\n"
"                P(Test1+,Test2+ | Disease-): %9$.4f<br>\n"
"                P(Test1+,Test2- | Disease-): %10$.4f<br>\n"
"                P(Test1-,Test2+ | Disease-): %11$.4f<br>\n"
"                P(Test1-,Test2- | Disease-): %12$.4f</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>The probability that a negative test result is a true negative:</p>"
msgstr "<p>Negatif bir test sonucunun gerçek bir negatif olma olasılığı:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>The probability that a positive test result is a true positive:</p>"
msgstr "<p>Pozitif bir test sonucunun gerçek bir pozitif olma olasılığı:</p>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>The radar plot's LR scale uses familiar likelihood-ratio evidence "
"categories described in the Users' Guides to the Medical Literature "
"(Jaeschke et al., 1994) solely as an illustrative visualization. Appropriate "
"thresholds and consequences depend on the clinical setting, population, "
"harms, benefits, and decision pathway.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/cotest.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>The two tests are run in parallel on the same subject and are assumed to "
"be <strong>conditionally independent</strong>: within the diseased group, "
"and again within the non-diseased group, the result of one test carries no "
"information about the other. The joint probabilities below are therefore "
"plain products of the entered sensitivities and "
"specificities.</p><p>Independence is the optimistic assumption. If the two "
"tests in fact tend to err together — same specimen, same operator, same "
"biology — it overstates how much the pair adds over either test alone. Clear "
"<em>Assume the two tests are conditionally independent</em> and enter a "
"dependence parameter to see how far the conclusion moves.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>This can be rewritten as:</p>"
msgstr "<p>Bu şu şekilde yeniden yazılabilir:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid "<p>To calculate how a test changes probability:</p>"
msgstr "<p>Bir testin olasılığı nasıl değiştirdiğini hesaplamak için:</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>You selected a <strong>parallel teaching strategy</strong>. Everyone "
"receives both {test1} (sensitivity {sens1}%, specificity {spec1}%) and "
"{test2} (sensitivity {sens2}%, specificity {spec2}%), and a final result is "
"positive when either test is positive.</p><p>The false-negative rates and "
"specificities therefore multiply. Combined sensitivity increases while "
"combined specificity decreases. These are the same accuracy formulas as "
"serial-negative testing; only second-test utilization differs. Tests that "
"fail on the same cases may add little benefit.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir <strong>paralel eğitim stratejisi</strong> seçtiniz. Herkes hem "
"{test1} (duyarlılık %{sens1}, özgüllük %{spec1}) hem de {test2} (duyarlılık "
"%{sens2}, özgüllük %{spec2}) alır ve nihai sonuç herhangi bir test pozitif "
"olduğunda pozitiftir.</p><p>Dolayısıyla yanlış negatiflik oranları ve "
"özgüllükler çarpılır. Birleşik duyarlılık artarken birleşik özgüllük azalır. "
"Bunlar seri negatif test ile aynı doğruluk formülleridir; yalnızca ikinci "
"test kullanımı farklıdır. Aynı olgularda başarısız olan testler çok az fayda "
"sağlayabilir.</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>You selected a <strong>serial-negative teaching strategy</strong>. "
"Everyone first receives {test1} (sensitivity {sens1}%, specificity "
"{spec1}%). Only first-test negatives receive {test2} (sensitivity {sens2}%, "
"specificity {spec2}%), and a final result is negative only when both tests "
"are negative.</p><p>The false-negative rates and specificities therefore "
"multiply. Combined sensitivity increases while combined specificity "
"decreases. Two negative results do not automatically rule disease out; NPV "
"still depends on prevalence, and false positives are shown in the "
"population-flow table.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir <strong>seri negatif eğitim stratejisi</strong> seçtiniz. Herkese "
"önce {test1} uygulanır (duyarlılık %{sens1}, özgüllük %{spec1}). Yalnızca "
"ilk testte negatif olanlara {test2} uygulanır (duyarlılık %{sens2}, özgüllük "
"%{spec2}) ve nihai sonuç yalnızca her iki test de negatif olduğunda "
"negatiftir.</p><p>Dolayısıyla yanlış negatiflik oranları ve özgüllükler "
"çarpılır. Birleşik duyarlılık artarken birleşik özgüllük azalır. İki negatif "
"sonuç hastalığı otomatik olarak dışlamaz; NÖD yine de prevalansa bağlıdır ve "
"yanlış pozitifler popülasyon akış tablosunda gösterilir.</p>"

#: R/sequentialtests.b.R
msgid ""
"<p>You selected a <strong>serial-positive teaching strategy</strong>. "
"Everyone first receives {test1} (sensitivity {sens1}%, specificity "
"{spec1}%). Only first-test positives receive {test2} (sensitivity {sens2}%, "
"specificity {spec2}%), and a final result is positive only when both tests "
"are positive.</p><p>The sensitivities and false-positive rates therefore "
"multiply. Combined specificity increases while combined sensitivity "
"decreases. Two positive results are not automatically a confirmed diagnosis; "
"PPV still depends on prevalence, and false negatives are shown in the "
"population-flow table.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Bir <strong>seri pozitif eğitim stratejisi</strong> seçtiniz. Herkese "
"önce {test1} uygulanır (duyarlılık %{sens1}, özgüllük %{spec1}). Yalnızca "
"ilk testte pozitif olanlara {test2} uygulanır (duyarlılık %{sens2}, özgüllük "
"%{spec2}) ve nihai sonuç yalnızca her iki test de pozitif olduğunda "
"pozitiftir.</p><p>Dolayısıyla duyarlılıklar ve yanlış pozitiflik oranları "
"çarpılır. Birleşik özgüllük artarken birleşik duyarlılık azalır. İki pozitif "
"sonuç otomatik olarak doğrulanmış bir tanı değildir; PÖD yine de prevalansa "
"bağlıdır ve yanlış negatifler popülasyon akış tablosunda gösterilir.</p>"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<span style='color:inherit;'><b>Significant difference detected.</b></span> "
"%1$s classified significantly more cases correctly than %2$s (accuracy "
"%3$.1f%% vs %4$.1f%%). McNemar's test compares overall correctness only; the "
"two tests may still differ in the sensitivity/specificity balance.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<strong>Cases where Test A and Test B have different CORRECTNESS</strong> "
"relative to the reference standard (e.g., Test A correct but Test B wrong, "
"or vice versa). McNemar's test examines whether the imbalance between these "
"discordant types is statistically significant. Exact inference is used "
"automatically when fewer than 25 discordant pairs are available, but "
"precision and power still depend on the number of discordant pairs."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<strong>Caution:</strong> No statistical comparison between the tests could "
"be computed for these data, so no test of one test against another was "
"performed; the reason is given in the Important Information panel. %s is "
"named here only because it had the highest observed balanced accuracy in "
"this sample, and these data say nothing about whether the tests differ.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<strong>Caution:</strong> No statistically significant difference was "
"detected between the tests compared. %s is named here only because it had "
"the highest observed balanced accuracy in this sample; the data neither "
"establish that it outperforms the others nor establish that the tests are "
"equivalent, since a non-significant result may simply reflect limited power. "
"The confidence intervals above show how large a real difference remains "
"compatible with these data.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"<strong>Compares diagnostic CORRECTNESS</strong> of two tests relative to "
"the gold standard. Focuses on <i>discordant pairs</i> (cases where one test "
"is correct and the other is wrong). Tests whether Test A correctly "
"classifies significantly more/fewer cases than Test B. Appropriate for "
"paired/matched data only. P < 0.05 indicates tests differ significantly in "
"accuracy."
msgstr ""

