"almost always means the marker is being read the wrong way round rather than "
"that it is useless: it separates the groups, but in the opposite direction "
"to the one assumed. Classification Direction is currently \"%2$s\"; "
"switching it to \"%3$s\" will give an AUC of 1 minus the value shown, with "
"sensitivity and specificity swapped accordingly. Change it only if that "
"matches what the marker means clinically."
msgstr ""

